  "scope": "Typed structural Match schema reuse and exact borrowed-retention versus materialization accounting.",
  "changes": [
    "Activation constructs private typed-source evidence from the genuine projection arena; runtime rechecks the actual retained owner and plan schema ID/key.",
    "Eligible structural Match values reuse existing projection schemas rather than rebuilding full source-owner closures and key indexes at each invocation. Unsupported owner-local and deep schema forms retain the original route.",
    "Borrowed retention measures actual container metadata and lengths while preserving exact encoded/retained bytes and nodes. Real comparisons, copying, finalization and result validation retain separate finite charges.",
    "Actual packed and zero-byte Unit sequence lengths bound expanded draft slots; maximum lexical intermediate depth bounds deep Values/Table payload copies before materialization.",
    "Metadata compute and comparison work propagate separately into enclosing retention meters. The certificate check allowance applies only to actual Snapshot paths that perform the check."
